  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, Expanded Withholding Tax (EWT) is required on payments to a VAT-registered law firm. This is in accordance with the provisions of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor businesses engaging the services of a VAT-registered law firm, it is essential to withhold the appropriate EWT from payments made. This ensures compliance with tax obligations and avoids potential penalties for non-compliance. The withheld amount must be remitted to the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) in accordance with the prescribed deadlines.",
